    "chunk_text": "Let us remember that a Budget is not merely a financial document, but a reflection of our moral and social priorities; it tells the people where we wish to take this country and what values we stand for, as leaders entrusted with their confidence.\n\nWe particularly welcome the Government\u2019s commitment to uplift the public sector and bring dignity back to the Public Service. The second stage of the public sector salary increase would be paid to all public servants from January, 2026. An amount of Rs. 110 billion has been provided for this. Also, the second stage of the pension revision for those who retired before 2020 would be paid from July, 2026, for which Rs. 20,000 million has been allocated. In addition, the interest-free festival advance, which stood at Rs. 10 000, has been increased to Rs. 15 000.\n\nThe nation welcomes the approval given to recruit 75,000 individuals to positions such as technical officers, law enforcement officers, revenue officers et cetera to maintain essential public services. What deserves\n\n1043 1044\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0db4\u0dc3\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0db4\u0dcf\u0db3\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dba\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0db4\u0dad\u0dcf\u0dad\u0daf]\n\n2025 \u0dc0\u0dba\u0daf\u0dc0\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca\u0db413\u0db4\n\napplause in this endeavour is that such recruitments and promotions would be carried out only in accordance with prescribed examinations and service requirements, free from political interference so as to provide equal opportunity to all."
  },
