    "md5": "46f864af769baa8fedc56efc03b7c962",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1074,
    "chunk_text": "applause in this endeavour is that such recruitments and promotions would be carried out only in accordance with prescribed examinations and service requirements, free from political interference so as to provide equal opportunity to all.\n\nThe allocation from the Budget, 2026 to make provision to continue with the Rs. 6,000 paid to a family towards expenses for stationery is commendable. It is a shot in the arm and an encouragement for the school children and their families.\n\nThe allocation of Rs. 11,000 million for improving the facilities and infrastructure of the medical faculties of the Sabaragamuwa, Ruhuna, Uva Wellassa and Eastern Universities is a move in the right direction. Then, the Proposal in the Budget, 2026 to increase the Mahapola allowance by a further Rs. 2,500 to what was granted in 2025, taking the total amount of what they would receive to Rs. 10,000 monthly is a great boost to our future generation of graduates and the educated class of this country. These, Sir, are long-term commitments that would shape the next generation of Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
