    "md5": "c1e6cc815779ef51a2eeb015e1fe29f9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1800,
    "chunk_text": "Now, when I made those comments, the Hon. Minister of Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources stood up and agreed with me. He would agree with that because he has been living in Jaffna for the last 15 or16 years, representing the JVP. He cannot say that what I said is a lie because then, he cannot go to Jaffna. You understand? So, naturally, the Hon. Minister, in a responsible way, agreed. But, to my surprise, the Hon. Deputy Minister of Defence, who is here - I started my comments today with this issue because he is here - stood up and denied it; when his speech came up soon after, he denied it saying that the military is very pure and that Gajendrakumar\n\nWe know that when he was in charge of the Eastern Province and when two police officers were killed at the Vavunativu checkpoint, the LTTE was accused. They tried to make out that it was former LTTE cadres who were trying to recreate the LTTE, which was an utter lie and he was the Commander of the Eastern Province at that time. Sir, I do not want to cast personal aspersions, but I am saying this with utmost responsibility.\n\nThis Government has our best wishes, this Government will have our entire support against the war on drugs and all other vices. But, I am telling you again, in the North and the East, without you dealing with the military's involvement in that, you will never get rid of that menace. And, I can tell you again, it is those retired military officers who are now involved in this strained drug menace in the South because you all did not deal with it in the last 17 years. It is now a menace even in the South. So, for God\u2019s sake, please make sure that Deputy Ministers of Defence do not whitewash what is essentially a cancer that started in the North and the East and is now spreading all over the country."
