    "chunk_size_bytes": 1660,
    "chunk_text": "This Government has our best wishes, this Government will have our entire support against the war on drugs and all other vices. But, I am telling you again, in the North and the East, without you dealing with the military's involvement in that, you will never get rid of that menace. And, I can tell you again, it is those retired military officers who are now involved in this strained drug menace in the South because you all did not deal with it in the last 17 years. It is now a menace even in the South. So, for God\u2019s sake, please make sure that Deputy Ministers of Defence do not whitewash what is essentially a cancer that started in the North and the East and is now spreading all over the country.\n\n1127 1128\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0db4\u0d8a.\u0d91\u0db8\u0dca.\u0db4\u0db6\u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dba\u0daf\u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db4\u0dad\u0dcf\u0dad\u0daf]\n\n2025 \u0dc0\u0dba\u0daf\u0dc0\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca\u0db413\u0db4\n\nNorthern Province has five districts and that comes to about Rs.1 billion per district. So, I asked the Divisional Secretaries of all those five districts what this Rs. 1 billion for roads amount to in practical terms. They said 20 kilometres of roads per district. So, this is what we are told as being having emphasis for the Northern Province and the Eastern Province. For the Eastern Province, there was nothing! There was just one sentence in the previous Budget: India will take care of the Eastern Province. In the Northern Province, we have the roads. The funniest part is, Jaffna got Rs.1 billion from that Budget and in the previous year under Ranil Wickremesinghe when the economy was even worse, Jaffna had Rs. 1.2 billion! So, actually, we had a Rs. 0.2 billion reduction. So, that is what happened last time."
