    "chunk_size_bytes": 1250,
    "chunk_text": "Northern Province has five districts and that comes to about Rs.1 billion per district. So, I asked the Divisional Secretaries of all those five districts what this Rs. 1 billion for roads amount to in practical terms. They said 20 kilometres of roads per district. So, this is what we are told as being having emphasis for the Northern Province and the Eastern Province. For the Eastern Province, there was nothing! There was just one sentence in the previous Budget: India will take care of the Eastern Province. In the Northern Province, we have the roads. The funniest part is, Jaffna got Rs.1 billion from that Budget and in the previous year under Ranil Wickremesinghe when the economy was even worse, Jaffna had Rs. 1.2 billion! So, actually, we had a Rs. 0.2 billion reduction. So, that is what happened last time.\n\nInstead, what do we have in this Budget? Only two times, something about the North or the East has been mentioned in this Budget, Sir, and that is with regard to the Lower Malwathu Oya Multipurpose Development Project, for which Rs. 5,000 million has been allocated primarily for the development of irrigation, land cultivation and agriculture of the Northern Province, particularly for the Mannar District. Rs. 5,000 million!"
