    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "7c9ff811d1f5c89a95c8fcc773242815",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1085,
    "chunk_text": "Instead, what do we have in this Budget? Only two times, something about the North or the East has been mentioned in this Budget, Sir, and that is with regard to the Lower Malwathu Oya Multipurpose Development Project, for which Rs. 5,000 million has been allocated primarily for the development of irrigation, land cultivation and agriculture of the Northern Province, particularly for the Mannar District. Rs. 5,000 million!\n\nThe other occasion where the North and the East are mentioned in this Budget is with regard to the development of four airports. Those airports are, Hingurakgoda, Sigiriya, Trincomalee and Jaffna. Sir, Rs. 1,000 million has been allocated for the development of those four airports. Jaffna is supposed to be an international airport and altogether, Rs. 1,000 million has been allocated. What does that mean? Rs. 250 million per airport. You will struggle even to build a luxury house in Colombo with the prices today. Here, we are talking about developing an airport and only Rs. 250 million has been allocated! Whom are you fooling? So, this has to change."
