    "chunk_text": "Initially, I would like to refer to the sudden eruption of communal tension pertaining to a temple being erected in Trincomalee. Several Hon. Members spoke before me about that. This is a very serious issue. Such issues come up all the time; from nowhere, suddenly, statues are brought and temples are erected and that creates unnecessary tension.\n\nNow, what has happened? Recently, one of my party members in the Colombo Municipal Council brought in a resolution regarding a Sabbat house. He asked the Mayor why she had not included his resolution regarding that Sabbat house, a place of religious worship that has been set up for the convenience of Jews, in Colombo. The Hon. Prime Minister very clearly said in the House that that is an unauthorized attempt to create a religious institution; she said so in the House. Finally, what happened? When that member from my party in the Colombo Municipal Council raised this issue, asking why they did not include it for debate in the Colombo Municipal Council, immediately the next day, he was called to the Terrorist Investigation Department and was asked to give a statement as to why he had raised this issue. When he asked why he had been summoned, they said, \"There are some Facebook comments about the motion you brought in at the Colombo Municipal Council.\" He said, \"This issue had been discussed in Parliament; the Hon. Prime Minister had said that it is an unauthorized structure. Therefore, it must be removed. So, why is the Colombo Municipal Council, which is the relevant authority for the removal of this institution, not taking action?\" Nothing had been done in that regard and whereas, he was summoned to the Terrorist Investigation Department, TID."
  },
