    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/22912_english_2025-11-17.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-11-17-2025-11-17-0203",
    "chunk_index": 203,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "ecc9e000c8a8e85e325241e2affd7c38",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1711,
    "chunk_text": "It is in that backdrop, Sir, that the Hon. Minister Ananda Wijepala was approached by several people and to his credit, whatever decisions that were taken yesterday were correct. That is what your Government came to power for, to stand by the law and ensure that there is no racism, but you backtracked. And today, that same Minister shamefully comes to this House, lies and says that the decisions taken yesterday were purely to protect that statue.\n\nAnd if you are to take your mandate seriously, that racist attitude was defeated promptly. One hundred and fifty nine Members got elected for you all on the basis that you all would not act the same way that they did. But, today, what you all have done is, you have capitulated. No, instead, what you must do is, you must go to the Sinhala people. The Sinhala people did not oppose yesterday when those actions were taken. Who opposed it? Goons. Goons from the outskirts of the Trincomalee\n\nDistrict were brought in. One of our Members of Parliament was assaulted by those very same goons. There are cases against those people. They were the ones who were brought in to create mayhem. The ordinary, Sinhala general public did not oppose it because they voted for you. They voted for the Hon. Tamil Member from Trincomalee who represents your party. So, it is your duty not to reverse and capitulate. On the contrary, what you must do is, you must go to the people and tell them the truth; you must explain to them what is right; you must explain to them the injustice that has been done. Instead of that, you have completely betrayed those Tamils and non-Sinhala voters who trusted you and voted for you. That is what you have done. So, Sir, this must change."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
