    "chunk_size_bytes": 1996,
    "chunk_text": "The Colombo Security Conclave comprising Sri Lanka, India, the Maldives, Mauritius and Bangladesh has developed into a vital regional architecture dedicated to safeguarding collective security across the Indian Ocean Region. Anchored on five core pillars - maritime safety, counter-terrorism, combating trafficking and transnational crime, cyber security and humanitarian assistance - the Conclave now represents a maturing framework where regional States pool resources, share expertise and jointly respond to emerging security challenges. Its recent institutionalization, including the establishment of the Secretariat in Colombo, marks a significant advancement from periodic consultations to a structured, cooperative security mechanism. It is noteworthy that Malaysia and Indonesia have also expressed interest in joining this regional initiative, further underscoring the Conclave\u2019s growing relevance.\n\nAt a time when narcotic inflows, cyber intrusions, transnational criminal activity and hybrid threats are rising, Sri Lanka must proactively utilize the full breadth of opportunities provided by the Colombo Security Conclave. I am sure, Sir, that you would understand that, at this moment, Sri Lanka is undergoing all those four threats I mentioned. So, my intention in asking this Question is to propose that we take maximum advantage of this opportunity before us.\n\nActive participation in its working groups and joint task forces, maritime operations and intelligence-sharing platforms would allow Sri Lanka to safeguard its territorial waters, protect its citizens, strengthen internal security and reinforce its role as a responsible and constructive partner in the Indian Ocean. The Conclave, therefore, serves not only as a regional mechanism, but also as a strategic avenue for Sri Lanka to enhance national security through practical cooperation with its trusted partners, especially India.\n\nIn this context, I wish to ask the Hon. Minister of Defence the following questions:"
