    "chunk_size_bytes": 2027,
    "chunk_text": "Active participation in its working groups and joint task forces, maritime operations and intelligence-sharing platforms would allow Sri Lanka to safeguard its territorial waters, protect its citizens, strengthen internal security and reinforce its role as a responsible and constructive partner in the Indian Ocean. The Conclave, therefore, serves not only as a regional mechanism, but also as a strategic avenue for Sri Lanka to enhance national security through practical cooperation with its trusted partners, especially India.\n\nIn this context, I wish to ask the Hon. Minister of Defence the following questions:\n\n2. What mechanisms currently exist for real-time intelligence sharing, particularly with India, combating narcotics trafficking, human smuggling, illegal fishing and other forms of transnational organized crime?\n\n3. Has Sri Lanka participated in any joint maritime operations, patrols, surveillance missions or coordinated exercises with the Colombo Security Conclave member States, including India, during the last three years? If so, please provide details and further inform this House when and where the next scheduled Colombo Security Conclave meeting, maritime exercise or senior officials\u2019 dialogue will take place.\n\n4. What steps are being taken to integrate Colombo Security Conclave technical platforms, information-sharing systems and operational\n\n437 438\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d86\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd. \u0d91\u0dda. \u0da2\u0dba\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0db0\u0db1 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0dc0\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0dda\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd 18\n\nframeworks into Sri Lanka\u2019s national security apparatus, particularly for maritime monitoring and narcotics interdiction?\n\nThis is the time that the Government of Sri Lanka is pursuing resolutely in order to achieve that.\n\n5. Has the Government formulated a national strategy or action plan to maximize Sri Lanka\u2019s contributions to and benefits from the Conclave\u2019s five pillars, particularly in collaboration with India and other member States, relating to counter-terrorism, cyber security and humanitarian assistance?"
