    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "fcf7b8a07bd08626026b9bf6335b8ad7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 834,
    "chunk_text": "It is because that single Ministry has been the cause for all the suffering that the Tamil people face, not only during the war, but even 16 years after the war. So, what are you going to do about it?\n\nThen, just another simple logical issue. The Hon. Deputy Minister of Defence and another JVP Member, who is a retired military officer, I guess, said what a great\n\nservice that the military, the Navy and the Air Force are doing in the North and the East.\n\nI think that comment was made because I had made reference to the ratio of the presence of the military establishment in the North and the East. In Jaffna, it is 1:14; in the Vanni, it is 1:2. So, with such an immense presence, to justify that, the Government benchers got up and said what a great service the military - the Army, the Navy and the Air Force - are doing there."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
