    "chunk_index": 233,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "c7bd4b9ef3f443839741702ff1e9e4c1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1647,
    "chunk_text": "Thank you, Sir. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Chairman) Next, the Hon. Shanakiyan Rajaputhiran Rasamanickam. You have 10 minutes.\n\n581 582\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0db1\u0dc0\u0daf\u0dba) \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0db8\u0db1\u0dcf\u0daf\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0d85\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0da0\u0dca\u0db1\u0db1\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0dc0\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0dda\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd 18\n\n[5.19 p.m.]\n\nI remember, the Hon. Prime Minister (Dr.) Harini Amarasuriya, when she was not even a Member of Parliament, before that also, advocated for an allocation of a minimum of 6 per cent of GDP for education. Now, she is in power; it is her Government that is in power and she is the Prime Minister. But, even under this Government, the Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education does not seem to have been given an allocation even close to that of the Ministry of Defence. So, these are matters that the Government needs to take notice of.\n\nThe security sector reform is something that we cannot overlook. I know the IMF conditions and I also know that the Government keeps talking about the IMF, blaming them for certain decisions that they have to take on taxation. But, security sector reform is also something that has been suggested. So, I would like to urge the Government to take into consideration, at least in the 2027 Budget, the excessive allocation that you keep making to the Defence Ministry and also the very small allocations you make to other Ministries. Those are matters that concern the entire country.\n\nBut, there are certain things that concern only the North and the East and the people of the North and the East."
  },
