    "chunk_id": "2025-11-20-2025-11-20-0102",
    "chunk_index": 102,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "c4bc91f79c40b2b518c9a7b5aa8a8c86",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1727,
    "chunk_text": "So, Sir, we must be able to absorb this into the economy. And also, the capital incentive part has to be encouraged. Capital absorption and the capital admission factor should be there and also, sensitivity and sincerity. On this particular basis, I state that the World Bank, JBIC, ADB and AIIB very clearly said that we have got to ensure that we move on to LNG. At that particular moment, they looked at Japan, India, USA, China and Pakistan and selected a company that does not produce LNG. Here, you must be politically sensitive. When production and our ports depend on China, when our trade depends on India and China, our Foreign Policy should be in line with the development of the country, the necessities of Sri Lanka and not for any other person's interests. So, India and China are very important; the USA is required for intentional relations; the European Union is needed for market access. You cannot sacrifice one for the other. So, that is why I say that political sensitivity has got to be looked at in all these, Sir. I am sure that these are matters you all should looked into when developing this country to be fast and robust in the future.\n\nSir, if we take the power plants, first, I looked at their generation part. But, now, we have got to ensure a proper retiring process for those plants.\n\n\u0dad\u0dc0\u0dad\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dab\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dad \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0db8 \u0dd2\u0dc4\u0db6\u0db8\u0dc0\u0dcf, \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0dca\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd2. \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0daf\u0dd4 50\u0d9a\u0da7 \u0db8\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dca \u0db4\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0d91\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dad\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca \u0db1\u0dcf\u0dd2\u0d9a \u0db4\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dad\u0dc2\u0dba \u0db4\u0da7\u0db1\u0dca \u0d9c\u0dad\u0dca\u0dad \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dad\u0dc4\u0da7\u0ddd\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dcf, \u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dca\u0db8\u0dc4 \u0db4, \u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca\u0dc4\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0db1\u0dd2\u0d9c\u0dbd, \u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca\u0da7\u0dd0\u0dc4\u0dda \u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dc4 \u0db1\u0dbd"
